   "comment_text": "NeuralFrame | Senior Backend Engineer, Medical Data Pipeline (Python + Rust) | REMOTE (US only, US time zones; no visa sponsorship) | Full-time | $170k–$210k + 0.1%–0.25% equity<p>We build software that hospitals, cancer registries and researchers use. You&#x27;d own the pipeline that pulls data from hospital systems and transforms it for analytics and research.<p>Where Rust fits: part of our hospital data acquisition layer, the code that talks to hospital systems, is written in Rust. You&#x27;d work on both sides: Rust where performance and correctness matter most, async Python for the rest of the pipeline. Rust experience is a strong plus. Whether you learned it at work or on your own, we want to hear what you built with it.<p>Stack: Rust, async Python (mypy, pytest, ruff, uv), PostgreSQL and MongoDB, Dagster, Terraform&#x2F;OpenTofu, AWS (ECS&#x2F;Fargate, RDS, Lambda, S3), GitHub Actions.<p>You&#x27;ll need 5+ years building backend services or data pipelines in production (retries, idempotency, schema design and migrations, well-tested and typed code) and strong Python and SQL. No healthcare background needed.<p>Apply: <a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;wellfound.com&#x2F;jobs&#x2F;4829721-senior-backend-software-engineer-medical-data-pipeline\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;wellfound.com&#x2F;jobs&#x2F;4829721-senior-backend-software-e...</a>. In your note, tell us in a few sentences about one pipeline failure you traced (what broke, how you found it, what you changed) and, if you&#x27;ve written Rust, what you built with it.",
